From a7f634c663ae5cdd20a93f6be7fb6e927c40f177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sound): decode native sound coordinates and update
 variants

Native 1.26.51.1 captures on protocol 2193 establish signed eighth-block positions and signed loop counts. Protocol 2225 replaces the seven repeated UpdateSoundData fields with one Event variant. Read its uint32 variant index and matching uint8 SoundDataEventType discriminator, then consume only that event payload. Mojang documents this change in the v1.26.60 release: https://github.com/Mojang/bedrock-protocol-docs/releases/tag/v1.26.60. Fade serializes duration before target volume.

Preserve Java fallback coordinates exactly and retain the native float listener-range gate. The 1.26.51.1 executable 537c0aee2e79afbdc94b44b28e00f466ae62bc50e2733d953b430db9dbaa9ee7 verifies the gate in function 144719f20. Keep native playback channels and resource archives in the following feature patch.
